{"name":"Cabbage Blossom Violet","hex":"#724c7b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cabbage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible plant (Brassica oleracea var. capitata) having a head of green leaves.\n\n Any of various cultivars of the species Brassica oleracea.","Any of various cultivars of the species Brassica oleracea."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form a head like that of the cabbage.","To do nothing; to idle; veg out."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabbage"},{"term":"blossom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flower, especially one indicating that a fruit tree is fruiting;  a mass of such flowers.","The state or season of producing such flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have, or open into, blossoms; to bloom.","To begin to thrive or flourish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom"},{"term":"violet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata;  similar-looking plants and flowers.","A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a violet colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cabbage","blocks":[{"text":"Cabbage, comprising several cultivars of Brassica oleracea, is a leafy green, red (purple), or white biennial plant grown as an annual vegetable crop for its dense-leaved heads. It is descended from the wild cabbage, and belongs to the \"cole crops\" or brassicas, meaning it is closely related to broccoli and cauliflower ; Brussels sprouts ; and Savoy cabbage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Cabbage_and_cross_section_on_white.jpg/330px-Cabbage_and_cross_section_on_white.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabbage","wikidata":"Q35051"},{"titl